{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/planarLayout()"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P0A7DrawingE12planarLayoutAD0C0Vy6VertexQzGSgyF","title":"planarLayout()","symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"planarLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drawing","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"PlanarLayout.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/GraphDrawing\/PlanarLayout.swift#L31"},"extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"GraphDrawing","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"roleHeading":"Instance Method"},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A crossing-free straight-line drawing on an integer grid, or nil when the graph is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"planar."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"planarLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Drawing","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"return-value","level":2,"text":"Return Value"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The drawing, in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order, or nil when the graph has no planar embedding."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The drawing comes from "},{"code":"planarEmbedding()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" by de Fraysseix, Pach and Pollack’s shift method"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in Chrobak and Payne’s linear-time form. The embedding of the underlying simple graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(self-loops and parallel copies drawn as one segment) is first made connected, by an edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the first vertex of each component to the first vertex of the next, and every face"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"boundary a simple cycle; then every face but the largest (the outer face) is triangulated."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The vertices are placed in a canonical ordering of that graph, each one above the contour"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of those before it, the contour shifted to make room. The added edges are not drawn and not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reported. Every vertex has integer coordinates with 0 ≤ x ≤ 2n − 4 and 0 ≤ y ≤ n − 2, and no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"two edges cross or overlap. Fewer than four vertices are placed at (0, 0), (2, 0) and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(1, 1) in "},{"code":"vertices","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" order. The drawing is not rescaled ("},{"code":"rescaled(scale:center:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" maps it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to a common frame). A directed graph is drawn through "},{"code":"undirectedView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"de Fraysseix, Pach and Pollack, “How to draw a planar graph on a grid”, Combinatorica"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"10(1), 1990."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Chrobak and Payne, “A linear-time algorithm for drawing a planar graph on a grid”,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Information Processing Letters 54(4), 1995.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"O(n + m) for the embedding, then O(n) expected (hashing the triangulation’s vertex pairs).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"As for ","type":"text"},{"code":"planarEmbedding()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Precondition","type":"aside","style":"note"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/graphprotocols\/graph\/planarlayout()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Vertex":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/vertex","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable"}],"title":"Vertex","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","abstract":[],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/GraphProtocols/Graph/planarLayout()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A crossing-free straight-line drawing on an integer grid, or nil when the graph is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"planar."}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/graphprotocols\/graph\/planarlayout()","title":"planarLayout()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"planarLayout","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12GraphDrawing0B0V","text":"Drawing","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/planarLayout()","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing":{"title":"GraphDrawing","url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing","kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/GraphProtocols":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/graphprotocols","title":"GraphProtocols","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols","abstract":[],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"title":"Graph","url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/graphprotocols\/graph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://GraphDrawing/documentation/GraphDrawing/Drawing":{"title":"Drawing","url":"\/documentation\/graphdrawing\/drawing","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphDrawing\/documentation\/GraphDrawing\/Drawing","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drawing"}],"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A position in the plane for each vertex, in a fixed vertex order: what every layout in this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module returns, and what a caller passes as a starting drawing."}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Drawing"}]}}}